# Authentication & Security Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Secure the Ingestion API and UI by implementing user authentication.
Currently, the API is open to anyone. We will add JWT-based authentication to the Go backend and a Login page to the Next.js frontend.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Go) - `services/ingestion`

#### [MODIFY] [main.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go)
-   Initialize `users` table in [main()](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#330-440) database connection block.
-   Add `AuthMiddleware` function to validate JWT tokens.
-   Wrap protected routes (`/submit`, `/scans`, etc.) with `AuthMiddleware`.
-   Add `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` endpoints.

#### [NEW] [auth.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/auth.go)
-   Define `User` struct.
-   Implement `RegisterHandler`: hashes password using `bcrypt`, saves user to DB.
-   Implement `LoginHandler`: verifies password, generates JWT token.
-   Implement `GenerateToken` and `ValidateToken` helper functions.

### Frontend (Next.js) - `ui`

#### [NEW] [ui/app/login/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/ui/app/login/page.tsx)
-   Create a login form with username and password fields.
-   Call `/auth/login` API on submit.
-   Store JWT token in `localStorage`.
-   Redirect to `/scans` on success.

#### [NEW] [ui/components/AuthProvider.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/ui/components/AuthProvider.tsx)
-   Context to manage auth state (user, token, login, logout).
-   Check for token on load.

#### [MODIFY] [ui/app/layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/ui/app/layout.tsx)
-   Wrap application with `AuthProvider`.

#### [MODIFY] [ui/app/scans/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/ui/app/scans/page.tsx)
-   Update `fetch` calls to include `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.
-   Handle 401 Unauthorized responses by redirecting to `/login`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
-   **API Test Script**: Create a script `scripts/test_auth.sh` to:
    1.  Register a new user.
    2.  Login and get a token.
    3.  Access a protected endpoint with the token (expect 200).
    4.  Access a protected endpoint without a token (expect 401).

### Manual Verification
-   **UI Testing**:
    1.  Open Chrome.
    2.  Navigate to `/scans`. Verify redirection to `/login`.
    3.  Enter credentials on `/login`.
    4.  Verify successful login and redirection back to `/scans`.
    5.  Verify data loads correctly.
